    "icons": "line",
    "rationale": "Anchor: Ledger (`compact rows, stark numerals, raised cards and still motion. Ledgers, invoicing, treasury.`) was picked over runner-up Realty for a government bank's ITPM/PSR hub -- its dense-tabular, still-motion register fits schedules, budgets, invoices and monthly PSR approvals, and its IBM Plex Sans body font matches the BRD's mandated typeface (BRD §11.3) verbatim without needing an override. hueShift -53 deliberately exceeds the usual +/-40 guardrail: BRD §9.8 ITPH-00296 is a hard MVP requirement ('the system shall use the Bank's visual identity -- logo and green colour palette'), and the approved prototype's CSS pins exact hex values (primary #2F7D32, brand #74BC44, sidebar #123A1C). The shift was solved by inverting the anchor's own HSL math to land primary at hue 122 -- identical to #2F7D32's hue -- so the app reads as LANDBANK green, not generic teal, while keeping Ledger's font pairing, radius (0.75rem) and shadow/motion character untouched. Archetype rail-dark renders the prototype's dark-green navigation rail (BRD 'Sidebar green -- Navigation background') via the anchor's own dark-mode palette (sidebarDark 146 10% 8%, a near-black desaturated green close to #123A1C) rather than a hand-picked color. Density stays at Ledger's default 'compact' -- PSR schedules, risk registers and financial tables are dense grids that need to stay legible at the BRD's required tablet/phone widths without excess scroll."
